                <pb facs="0908" n="780" xml:id="pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./64:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-02T12:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1928—12
                                noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. Upon instruction of the Pan American Airways, MacGregor left today via San
                    Salvador for Tegucigalpa to open negotiations for transport concession.</p>
                <p>The Government here is indisposed to take action on the company’s application
                    while the Cabinet resignations are pending. Repeated to Tegucigalpa and San
                    Salvador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
